diff --git a/PHASE_4_NOTES.md b/PHASE_4_NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e444204
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PHASE_4_NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# PHASE 4 NOTES
+
+## Base state (read this first)
+
+The zip given for Phase 4 still contained **unresolved git merge conflict markers** (`<<<<<<< HEAD`) in 7 Python
+files and `requirements.txt`, committed in HEAD. Nothing imported. They are resolved as **Part 0**
+(`signalpost-phase4-part0-conflicts.patch`): always the HEAD side, which is byte-identical (EOL-normalised) to
+commit `978e036` (Phase 3). Baseline after Part 0: `pytest tests` = 77 passed.
+Not touched (out of scope, still contain markers): `README.md`, `docs/*.md`, `entry-companies.jsonl`,
+`out/latest-run/*` sample artifacts (incl. `request-log.jsonl`, `profiles.jsonl`, `all-orgs.txt`).
+
+## Answers U1 to U8
+
+- U1 Log line fields: timestamp, run_id, organisation_number, module, provider, operation, event_type, caller_module, success, http_status, duration_ms, cache_hit, cache_miss, attempt, retry, [error], [retry_reason], failure_class. **No bytes, no cost, no connector.** The spec's "requests_by_connector" and per-line cost formula did NOT exist; `build_metrics` only had by_provider / by_module. Added: optional `bytes` and `cost_usd` on log lines, `connector_for()`, `event_cost_usd()`, and run-level `requests.by_connector / bytes / third_party_cost_usd`, all from the same helpers.
+- U2 Every attempt (including retries) already wrote its own log line (`attempt`, `retry`). One line = one HTTP attempt. Retries count as requests, consistently everywhere.
+- U3 Scrapy did NOT write to the request log. Fixed: `OperationalTelemetryMiddleware` now logs each response/exception (org from `request.meta`; Scrapy's own robots.txt requests have no meta, so the host is mapped to the company that first requested it; unmapped = null org and shows up as unattributed).
+- U4 OCR PDF download used raw `urllib`, unlogged. Fixed: logged as module `annual_report_pdf`, provider BRREG, with bytes. It is **not** covered by the rate limiter (raw urllib, outside `fetch_json`).
+- U5 `output_contract._operations()` returned 3 keys (requests, runtime_ms, third_party_cost_usd). Now returns 7 keys. `schema_version` stays "1.0": the validator checks the constant, no bump was forced. `tests/test_phase3_envelope.py` asserted the 3-key set; updated to the new shape (intentional).
+- U6 The rate-limited endpoint in `official._fetch_history()` is `BRREG_ACCOUNT_YEARS` = `data.brreg.no/regnskapsregisteret/regnskap/aarsregnskap/kopi/{org}/aar`. Rule matches that path only (not the PDF copy path, not other BRREG endpoints). `_fetch_history`/`_reserve_history_slot` in official.py left untouched (dead code, out of scope).
+- U7 No file locking, only an in-process `threading.Lock`. Fine: stages are sequential processes. Same approach for `company-spans.jsonl`.
+- U8 Stage 4 extractors and 5b make no HTTP calls (no `urlopen`/`record_request` in them). No change.
+
+Other finding (not fixed): `telemetry.read_events()` raises on any malformed log line, so a corrupt log crashes the end of `run_agent`. `build_operations_by_org` is tolerant (counts `malformed`).
+
+## Baseline 429 count (Step 0)
+
+Shipped sample `out/latest-run/request-log.jsonl`: 299 parsable lines (+3 conflict-marker lines), statuses 200: 260, 404: 39, **429: 0**.
+Therefore `brreg_history` ships with `min_interval_s = 0.0` (spacing OFF). 429 handling is always on. Zero 429 in one run proves only that it was not hit, not that the 30/min limit does not exist.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `telemetry.py`: `company_context`, `current_organisation`, `company_span`, `record_request(bytes_received, cost_usd, org fallback)`, `connector_for`, `event_cost_usd`, `summarize_requests`, `build_operations_by_org`, `reconcile_operations_report`, `empty_operations`.
+- `rate_limit.py` (new, no internal imports): `RateLimiter` (burst 1), `limiter_for`, `parse_retry_after`, `SIGNALPOST_RATE_LIMITS`.
+- `http.py`: limiter per attempt; 429 honours `Retry-After` (cap 120 s, else current backoff), penalizes the shared limiter, retries inside the existing 3-attempt budget; exhausted 429 gives `error="HTTP 429 rate_limited"` which becomes the evidence note. 404/410 unchanged. Bytes logged on every line that has a body.
+- Stage 1 `collect_profile` is now a wrapper entering `company_context` + `company_span("registry")` inside the worker, around the renamed `_collect_profile_inner` (incl. its except path).
+- Tavily/Exa: context + span around the search call and the candidate `fetch_website`; `cost_usd` and bytes on the log line (Exa `costDollars.total`; Tavily `usage.credits x TAVILY_USD_PER_CREDIT`, same formula as `discovery.py`, 0 when no usage block).
+- OCR connector: `collect_attributed` worker wrapper (context + span), PDF download logging.
+- Stage 6 (`build_output_contract.py`): loads operations once; `--request-log/--spans-log/--operations-report`; no log = zeros, `source: "unavailable"`; writes `operations-report.json`. `run_agent.py` sets `SIGNALPOST_SPANS_LOG`, passes the paths, and completes the report with `reconcile_operations_report` after `run-metrics.json` exists (stage 6 runs before it). `run.py` copies the report to `result/`.
+- `validate_envelopes.py`: operations keys/types checked inside the existing keyset check (no new check name).
+- `scripts/validate_operations.py`, `tests/test_phase4_*.py`, `.env.example`.
+
+## Honest limits
+
+- `result/operations-report.json` `uncovered_stages` is `[]` because Scrapy and PDF downloads are now logged. Only unit-tested (fake request/response objects); **never run against a real Scrapy crawl here**.
+- **The full pipeline was NOT run.** No network to BRREG/Tavily/Exa in the build sandbox. Checks 3-5 and 7-8, 11 were run on shipped sample data (9 of 20 profiles survived the mangled sample file, log filtered to those 9 orgs, bytes/cost synthetic): all pass, `reconciled: true`. Check 9 skipped (no interval). Check 11 on a real 20-org run: **still to do on your machine**.
+- Check 6 (context leak) cannot be proven from a log: lines have no URL. Covered by the 12-thread/100-task unit test, which would fail if the context leaked.
+- Check 10 is covered by pytest with a stubbed `urlopen`, not a real fake HTTP server.
+- Tavily cost is 0 unless the API response includes `usage.credits` and `TAVILY_USD_PER_CREDIT` is set.
+- Retry cost under Phase 2 resume is counted, not de-duplicated (as specified).
+- Fat format (`--envelope-format fat`) gets no `operations`.
+- `runtime_ms` only exists for stages that open a span: registry, discovery, workforce_ocr. Scrapy crawl wall-clock is not attributed per company (Twisted, shared concurrency).
+
+## Commands (this sandbox)
+
+```
+PYTHONPATH=src python -m pytest tests -q        # before: 77 passed (after Part 0) | after: 96 passed
+python scripts/validate_operations.py --run-dir <dir> --envelopes <envelopes.jsonl>
+python run.py --organisations entry-companies.jsonl       # run this yourself; needs network
+```
